        "id": "d6d45e03ec9bc23385c9b75111f7fe2a31d6ba63",
        "tree_id": "9aa9c55141d5928dc16cf5de854bb4cf0d33b65f",
        "message": "feat(NET-003): authoritative rooms on the pinned ws transport\n\nA0004 records the Director's verbatim instruction: 'bypass pin colyseus'.\nNET-003 therefore uses ws 8.23.0, already pinned and audited in STACK.lock:\nno dependency added, no lockfile change. The stale Colyseus line stays as a\nrecord; a future decision may restore it without rewriting room lifecycle.\n\nRoom is transport-agnostic: a socket is anything with send(Uint8Array), and\nws-adapter.ts is the only ws boundary. OPEN -> DRAINING -> CLOSED lifecycle;\nresume handles reclaim the original entity inside a 30-tick window and are\nFNV-1a tamper detectors, not credentials (SEC-001 owns auth). Resume sends a\nsnapshot and never replays intents server-side, which would double-apply.\n\nReplayed intents used to be silently dropped at tick time by SimHost; Room now\nrefuses them at ingress with a reason event.\n\nGDD-SHARDING 0.2 -> 0.3 (I9) including its corrupted open-questions table.\nNET-003's acc repaired to the test file; 9 broken accs remain. D146's generator\nwas re-run against the new metrics (60 commands, 8 evidence dirs).\n\nAcceptance: rooms 17/17, server 25/25, full 90/90, verify 17/17, typecheck 0,\ncore-math 0, tracer green.\n\nAgent: backend-engineer\nTask: NET-003",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-18T08:59:37Z",
